2. The only question which has to be answered by this Court is, whether Order 41 Rule 31 is mandatory and if so what are the parameters of this Rule. Rule 31 of Order 41 states;
"Order 41 Rule 31

Contents, date and signature of judgment - The judgment of the appellate Court shall be in writing and shall state -
(a) the points for determination;
(b) the decision thereon;
(c) the reasons for the decision; and
(d) where the decree appealed from is reversed or varied, the relief to which the appellant is entitled;
and shall at the time that it is pronounced be signed and dated by the Judge or by the Judges concurring therein."
As a matter of fact there cannot be any dispute that the judgment of appellate Court should be in writing and should also state the points of determination and decision thereon. The judgment shall also state the reasons for the decision and as such, we do not think that the rule is not mandatory.

